cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this VALENCE software release and the associated paper when available."
title: "VALENCE: Validator Availability and Latency Emulator for Network Consensus Evaluation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Harris"
    given-names: "Chris"
    affiliation: "University of Northern Colorado"
version: 0.8.1
date-released: 2026-08-02
license: MIT
keywords:
  - blockchain
  - proof-of-stake
  - consensus
  - distributed systems
  - network latency
  - discrete-event simulation
abstract: >-
  VALENCE is a deterministic discrete-event simulator for evaluating how
  latency tails, temporal dependence, correlated disruption, validator outages,
  gossip topology, stake distribution, validator resource constraints, and
  version-pinned Ethereum-calibrated validator duties affect Proof-of-Stake
  consensus.
